Fish: Fish game rules in the in-world Game Rules screen (P8.10).

The screen lists `RULES`, a const table of rules with a two-valued `Value`, and edits them through
private state (`numbers`, `values`, `initial`), so no horizon-mixins hook can add rows to it. This
patch lets `RulesScreen::with_fish` add the rules mods registered: a switch for a boolean rule, a
number box for an integer or decimal one, a button cycling the choices of an enum one, each in the
rule's category. Done writes the changed ones through `fish_hooks` (`game_rule_set`). Only the
screen of a world this game runs has them: the call in `lan_screen.rs` passes the world's id, which
is `None` for a remote server. Create New World's screen is untouched. It needs the bundle applied
(`fish_bridge::rules::world_of`).

